[22.328637, "o", "# environment/disk.tar.gz is produced by build_disk.py"]
[22.328654, "o", "\r\n\r\nRun `python3 build_disk.py tasks/<range>` after generation to synthesise the forensic image here (+ sha256) and augment `sas-mock/` with the CTI/handoff materials. The Docker build (context = this directory) bakes it read-only at `/disk`; `sas-mock/` is baked at `/sas`.\r\n\r\nEvery path cited in `tests/manifest.json` must exist inside the image (QA gate: manifest ↔ disk 100%).\r\n"]
[22.328877, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[22.328942, "o", "root@cf898cdca5d7:/app# "]
[37.931861, "i", "head -n 50 /app/task/tests/rewardkit/runner.py /app/task/tests/rewardkit/judge.py\n"]
[37.932183, "o", "head -n 50 /app/task/tests/rewardkit/runner.py /app/task/tests/rewardkit/judge.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[37.932535, "o", "==> /app/task/tests/rewardkit/runner.py <==\r\n"]
[37.932638, "o", "\"\"\"The scoring loop: import criterion files, evaluate instances, apply gates, aggregate.\r\n"]
[37.932715, "o", "\r\nDirectory → reward-key mapping mirrors the design (doc 02 §2.1, §3.6):\r\n  structure/  → structure gate (required_pass, multiplicative)\r\n  grounding/  → grounding rate + fabrication gate\r\n  detection/  → `detection` axis (discovery, silent_recall[w=0], chain, no_cve, attribution)\r\n  planning/   → `plan` axis (coverage, verification, ordering, plan-quality judge)\r\n  quality/    → `quality` key (Q-dimension judge; eval-only by default)\r\n\"\"\"\r\nfrom __future__ import annotations\r\n\r\nimport importlib.util\r\nimport json\r\nimport os\r\nimport sys\r\nfrom pathlib import Path"]
[37.932758, "o", "\r\n\r\nimport rewardkit as rk\r\nimport rewardkit.judge as judgemod   # dotted form: the module __getattr__ registrar shadows\r\n                                     # `from rewardkit import judge` (it returns a function)\r\n\r\nGROUPS = [\"structure\", \"grounding\", \"detection\", \"planning\", \"quality\"]\r\nGROUP_TO_REWARD = {\"planning\": \"plan\"}          # others map to their own name\r\nLATE = (\"discovery.py\", \"verification.py\")      # generated instance-registration files\r\nTHRESHOLD = 0.70                                # per-axis pass threshold (doc 01 §4.6)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _reward_key(group: str) -> str:\r\n    return GROUP_TO_REWARD.get(group, group)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _load(path: Path, name: str):\r\n    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(name, str(path))\r\n    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\r\n    sys.modules[name] = mod\r\n    spec.loader.exec_module(mod)\r\n    return mod\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _wmean(pairs):\r\n    num = sum(w * s for w, s in pairs)\r\n    den = sum(w for w, _ in pairs)\r\n    return round(num / den, 4) if den else None\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _parse_reward_toml(path: Path) -> list:\r\n    \"\"\"Tiny purpose-built parser for reward.toml ([[reward]] name/aggregation) — avoids a TOML\r\n    dependency so the deterministic path runs on stock Python 3.9.\"\"\"\r\n    blocks, cur = [], None\r\n    for raw in path.read_text().splitlines():\r\n\r\n==> /app/task/tests/rewardkit/judge.py <==\r\n\"\"\"Tier-3 judge adapter.\r\n\r\nReads a judge TOML ([judge] + [[criterion]] blocks) and, for each criterion, asks the judge\r\nmodel to score the agent's report against the ground-truth manifest. Binary → 0/1; likert-N →\r\n(score-1)/(points-1) in [0,1].\r\n\r\nProvider is chosen by REWARDKIT_JUDGE = \"<provider>/<model>\":\r\n  - anthropic/<model>  → Anthropic Messages API   (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY)   e.g. anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5\r\n  - gemini/<model>     → Gemini generateContent    (GEMINI_API_KEY)      e.g. gemini/gemini-2.5-flash\r\nA bare \"<model>\" with no provider is treated as anthropic.\r\n\r\nJudge hygiene (doc 02 §3.5): the judge family MUST differ from the policy family. When the\r\nagents under evaluation are Claude, use a gemini/* judge; when they are Gemini, use an\r\nanthropic/* judge.\r\n\r\nThe judge is OPTIONAL and degrades cleanly: if REWARDKIT_JUDGE is unset, the provider is\r\nunknown, or the matching key is missing, every criterion is returned `skipped` (excluded from\r\nthe axis mean) — the deterministic-only path selftest exercises. Calls use stdlib urllib (no\r\nSDK dependency); API keys go in headers, never in URLs or logs.\r\n\"\"\"\r\nfrom __future__ import annotations\r\n\r\nimport json\r\nimport os\r\nimport urllib.request\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nANTHROPIC_URL = \"https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages\"\r\nANTHROPIC_VERSION = \"2023-06-01\"\r\nGEMINI_URL = \"https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/{model}:generateContent\"\r\n\r\ntry:  # TOML reader — stdlib on 3.11+, optional backport otherwise\r\n    import tomllib as _toml\r\nexcept ModuleNotFoundError:  # pragma: no cover\r\n    try:\r\n        import tomli as _toml  # type: ignore\r\n    except ModuleNotFoundError:\r\n        _toml = None\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _skipped(criteria, reason):\r\n    return {\"criteria\": [{\"name\": c, \"weight\": w, \"score\": None,\r\n                          \"skipped\": True, \"reason\": reason} for c, w in criteria]}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _judge_target():\r\n    \"\"\"Return (provider, model, key) if a usable judge is configured, else None.\"\"\"\r\n    spec = os.environ.get(\"REWARDKIT_JUDGE\", \"\").strip()\r\n    if not spec:\r\n        return None\r\n"]
